# RadioReach — Cloudflare Pages redirects
#
# The app is a single page that uses hash routing (e.g. /#/success), so there
# are NO client-side path routes that need an SPA rewrite. A catch-all
# `/* /index.html 200` would make every unknown URL return the homepage with a
# 200 status (soft 404s + duplicate content, all canonicalising to "/").
# Instead unknown paths serve the real 404 page with a 404 status.

# Canonicalise legacy / alternate paths
/index.html            /                                          301
/resources             /resources/                                301
/privacy               /privacy-policy/                           301
/privacy.html          /privacy-policy/                           301
/terms.html            /terms/                                    301

# Old (2 MB) share image → optimised JPEG, so previously-scraped OG cards resolve
/images/radioreach-share-v2.png   /images/radioreach-share-v2.jpg            301
/images/studio.jpg                /images/studio-1280.jpg                    301

# Everything else that does not match a static asset is a genuine 404
/*                     /404.html                                  404
